    h1 { AI 2026 }

    Where we are, and where we aren't
}
hr {}

section#intro {
It's October 2026. Or at least, it was when I began writing this. OpenAI has just released a[href=https://openai.com/index/sharing-ai-progress-in-mathematics/]{a massive github repo of of .pdf and .lean files}.

There are more than 700 PDFs, and some portion of those results also come with Lean certificates.

This has led to quite a bit of discussion. Is it the end of human mathematics? Is it time to move to a "math 2.0"? Is AGI here? Or ASI? The eschaton?

With all the commentary flying around, much of it quite bombastic, I figured I should go ahead and make a record of where my head was at at this time. I don't intend this as a persuasive piece, more of a snapshot of my thoughts.
}

$contents {}

$contentsEntry[intro|numberless]{
    Introduction
}

